## 🔬 Research Overview

This division explores the human brain, nervous system, neural signals, and technologies that connect biological systems with computers.

The goal is to understand how the brain works and explore how brain-computer interfaces can enable new forms of human-computer interaction.

## 🧬 Research Areas

| Field | Focus |
|---|---|
| 🧠 Neuroscience | Brain structure and function |
| ⚡ Neural Signals | Electrical activity of neurons |
| 🔌 Brain-Computer Interfaces | Communication between brain and computers |
| 📊 EEG Analysis | Understanding brainwave signals |
| 🤖 Computational Neuroscience | Mathematical models of neural systems |
| 🧪 Cognitive Science | Learning, memory, and perception |
| 🦾 Neurotechnology | Technology interacting with the nervous system |

## 🎯 Research Objectives

- Study the fundamentals of neuroscience.
- Understand neurons and neural communication.
- Explore EEG signals and brainwave patterns.
- Learn the principles of brain-computer interfaces.
- Experiment with neural signal processing.
- Investigate the relationship between AI and neuroscience.

## 🧪 Experiments & Investigations

Experiments and learning projects will be documented here.

Each investigation should include:
- Research question
- Background and references
- Methodology
- Equipment and software
- Observations and results
- Limitations and future improvements

